 "notes": {
  "method": "Muristan block (Greek Orthodox market, 1900s): 2 storeys of honey-cream ashlar, ground-floor round-arched shopfronts with fanlights and teal/green steel doors or grey roll-downs, upper floor of round-arched windows and small balconies with black railings (notes 1.6, 1.7, 2.6; F01 from the Redeemer tower shows the blocks and their long red-tile hipped roofs).",
  "e3": "east face on the fountain square (D01 right, D08 left): shops under awnings, upper round-arched windows with two balconies (black railings).",
  "e2": "south-east face on the SW lane (D04 left, cam (211.9,63.6)): pale grey-green steel doors and grey roll-downs, a steel shed canopy on big green hoop brackets, ATM kiosk; upper wall with few windows.",
  "e0": "west face on the 6 m west lane: no photo; market-lane profile (rules).",
  "height": "2 storeys, eaves ~10 m (F01).",
  "roof": "Real roof: red-tile hipped (F01, F03, D07, D08). Left flat here: build_city's hip roof uses the oriented bounding box and would overhang this footprint by metres (profile request). 'domes': 1 where set only keeps the vernacular lime-dome field (5-8 domes) off a roof that is really tiled."
 },
